<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cosimo I de' Medici</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1519">1519</a>–<a href="/years/1574">1574</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cosimo I de' Medici became duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> at seventeen after the murder of his cousin Alessandro in 1537. He crushed the republican exiles at Montemurlo, conquered Siena in the 1550s with Spanish backing and built a centralised state, commissioning the Uffizi from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giorgio-vasari">Giorgio Vasari</a>. In 1569 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-v">Pope Pius V</a> made him the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duke-of-tuscany">Grand Duke of Tuscany</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cosimo-i-de-medici.jpg" alt="Cosimo I de' Medici" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bronzino · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Agnolo_Bronzino_-_Cosimo_I_de%27_Medici_in_armour_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
